{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate overnight street lighting & make councils liable if they fail to comply ",
        "additional_details": "Many local councils are turning off streetlights to cut budgets, creating dark zones that leave residents feeling unsafe. Under the current law, local authorities face no legal liability if a member of the public is injured or targeted by criminals in these blackouts. We believe this system prioritises saving money over protecting people, especially shift workers and vulnerable groups. The Government must change the law to hold councils more accountable for public safety.",
        "background": "Change the law to give councils a legal duty to keep streetlights lit at night. Currently, they have no duty to do so and face no liability if turning lights off to cut costs leads to preventable crimes or accidents. Public safety must come first.",
